<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 3 August, from 8 to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">8</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tiberius defeats the Pannonian rebels at the River Bathinus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roman forces under Tiberius defeated the rebel Breuci at the River Bathinus, and their leader Bato surrendered. It was a turning point in the great Illyrian revolt against Roman rule.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1492</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sets sail from Palos on his first voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Christopher Columbus left Palos de la Frontera with the Niña, Pinta and Santa María, seeking a westward route to Asia. Ten weeks later he reached the Bahamas.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1778</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">La Scala opera house opens in Milan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Teatro alla Scala opened with Salieri's opera L'Europa riconosciuta. It became one of the world's leading opera houses, closely linked with Verdi, Puccini and Toscanini.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1914</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Germany declared war on France and prepared to strike through neutral Belgium under the Schlieffen Plan. The invasion of Belgium the next day brought Britain into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan">Schlieffen Plan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1936</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jesse Owens wins the 100 metres at the Berlin Olympics</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jesse Owens won the 100 metres, the first of four gold medals at the Berlin Games. The success of a Black American athlete undercut Nazi propaganda about racial superiority.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1981</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US air traffic controllers go on strike</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nearly 13,000 members of the PATCO union walked out. President Reagan gave them 48 hours to return; he then fired more than 11,000, a defining moment for American labour relations.</p></li></ol>
